-### Algorithm Steps
-1.  Sample $N$ points $\{\mathbf{p}_i = \mathbf{o} + z_i \mathbf{r}\}$ along camera ray $\mathbf{r}$ [S1].
-2.  Input point $\mathbf{p}$ into geometry MLP $f_g$ to predict SDF $d_\Omega(\mathbf{p})$ and geometry feature $\mathbf{F}_g$ [S1].
-3.  Input $\mathbf{p}$, view direction $\mathbf{r}$, and $\mathbf{F}_g$ into SRDF MLP $f_s$ to predict SRDF $\tilde{d}_\Omega(\mathbf{p}, \mathbf{r})$ [S1].
-4.  Compute volume density $\sigma^{\text{SRDF}}(\mathbf{p}, \mathbf{r})$ using the formula above [S1].
-5.  Compute color $\mathbf{c}$ using $f_c$ with inputs $\mathbf{r}, \mathbf{F}_g, \mathbf{p}, \mathbf{n}=\nabla d_\Omega(\mathbf{p})$ [S1].
-6.  Render color $\mathbf{C}(\mathbf{r})$, depth $D$, and normal $\mathbf{N}$ using standard volume rendering equations with $\sigma^{\text{SRDF}}$ [S1].
-7.  Compute losses (Color, Depth, Normal, Eikonal, Smooth, Consistency, Visibility) and update network weights [S1].
-8.  **Post-Training:** Extract watertight mesh from $d_\Omega(\mathbf{p})$ using Marching Cubes [S1].
+### Pseudocode
+```python
+def srdf_volume_render(ray_origin, ray_direction, N, fg, fs, fc, alpha, beta):
+    # 1. Sample points along the ray
+    points = [ray_origin + (i / N) * ray_direction for i in range(N)]
+    
+    # 2. Forward pass through networks
+    sdf_vals = []
+    features = []
+    normals = []
+    colors = []
+    
+    for p in points:
+        # Geometry MLP
+        d_p, Fg = fg(p)
+        sdf_vals.append(d_p)
+        features.append(Fg)
+        
+        # Compute normal from SDF gradient (approximated or via autograd)
+        n = normalize(grad(d_p, p))
+        normals.append(n)
+        
+        # SRDF MLP
+        d_srdf = fs(concat(ray_direction, Fg, p))
+        
+        # Color MLP
+        c = fc(concat(ray_direction, Fg, p, n))
+        colors.append(c)
+        
+        # Compute density from SRDF
+        psi = laplace_cdf(-d_srdf, beta)
+        sigma = alpha * psi
+        alpha_i = 1.0 - exp(-sigma * (1.0 / N))
+        T_i = prod(1.0 - alpha_j for j in range(i))
+        
+    # 3. Accumulate color, depth, normal
+    C = sum(T_i * alpha_i * c for i, c in enumerate(colors))
+    D = sum(T_i * alpha_i * z_i for i, z_i in enumerate(points))
+    N_out = sum(T_i * alpha_i * n for i, n in enumerate(normals))
+    
+    return C, D, N_out
+```
 
